  "body": "## Reproduced and published; actual-merge certification pending\n\nv16.49 tests a binary root joining two nontrivial chain subtrees. Independent proof review accepts the interface construction: overlapping palettes retain a common anchor; disjoint palettes are normalized separately and exchanged as complete label roles, preserving inner profiles while only the parent can carry a unit deficit. The scoped theorem covers one binary parent with two internal-chain children of arbitrary finite lengths/degrees. Arbitrary retained-tree universality remains unresolved.\n\n- Verified integrated parent: `0c0efebe7f1b6c0eafbde744621f7b1f7bef117e`.\n- Immutable prospective protocol: `9c9aeaeeda6d11f4aba4c472a3325a3de86af423`, direct child of that parent.\n- [Prospective RED run](https://github.com/proteinfoldingengine/WetLabEngine/actions/runs/36860768895) at `02adc0cf7aa44d0836d951c87ccdd7e804131b5d`: expected missing-interface and coverage assertions observed before implementation; raw archive retained.\n- Reviewed scientific source: `c7c05ab500a6be1d9a7bd1e116133de650f18736`.\n- [Full scientific execution and independent reproduction](https://github.com/proteinfoldingengine/WetLabEngine/actions/runs/36861656790): all jobs SUCCESS, including evidence publication.\n- Outcome **FORK_CHAIN_INTERFACE_VALIDATED**: 133 representative normalizations and 192 directed cases pass; zero construction failures and zero nonunit pairs.\n- Complete frozen graphs at k2,k3: 430,250 states, 3,113,250 primitive edges, 31 profiles and 809 component pairs.\n- The 11-vertex fork is smallest with both child chains having at least two internal vertices; it is not the smallest internally branching tree. Larger-palette directed cases are not exhaustive universes.\n- 934 passing checks: 845 inherited + 89 new. Full fresh parent48/nested science; all33 scientific files reproduce byte-for-byte.\n- 88 execution manifest members; 1,722 source/input paths bound to1,429 unique source objects and exact Git blobs.\n\nPrimary B1/Binf/Bs remain independent scalar minima; LEX is separate. General quantification rests on the reviewed proof, not finite enumeration. Publication byte audit passed: 232 manifest entries, full raw archives and source bindings verified, with scientific execution on separate concurrent runners. Exact-head merge is complete at `a8280c1c77d7e29f8b90dfd4807bede6411c7ca7`; ordered parents and publication-tree equality are verified. [Actual-merge replay](https://github.com/proteinfoldingengine/WetLabEngine/actions/runs/36863457271) and an independently audited durable receipt remain required before CLOSED/CERTIFIED.\n\n\nReviewed publication head: `73270dff8a5832b936d186246fbf43b952590936`; tree `687f0ae2981b032aae44a36e68ebd3a869d83ad9`.\n",
